{
  "version": 2,
  "description": "Provider-neutral role policy. Resolve with scripts/resolve-model-routing.sh, then copy the result to RUN_DIR/model-routing.json.",
  "default_runtime": "claude",
  "host_policy": {
    "claude": {
      "allowed_spawn_models": [
        "haiku",
        "sonnet",
        "opus",
        "fable"
      ],
      "forbidden": [
        "premium"
      ],
      "note": "haiku/sonnet/opus defaults; fable available for escalation tiers (frontier/escalated) only \u2014 re-enabled Jul 2026. haiku is the cheap rung (Scoot). Fable is not a review-gate default: cold reviewers run on the tier that differs from the author (Robin, 2026-09-16); fable is reached by the bounce rule's second rung, an active experiment, or an explicit human ask, and every fable spawn needs a hand-written MODEL-OVERRIDE reason (preflight-artifacts.sh --phase final, fable-override)."
    },
    "openai": {
      "allowed_spawn_models": [
        "gpt-5.6-terra",
        "gpt-5.6-sol",
        "gpt-6-astra"
      ],
      "allowed_exec_models": [
        "gpt-5.3-codex-spark"
      ],
      "forbidden": [],
      "note": "Codex host: native subagent spawns use gpt-5.6-terra or gpt-5.6-sol by default; gpt-6-astra is reserved for the escalated tier. gpt-5.3-codex-spark is allowed only through the granular-ui-fast one-shot exec profile. Pass model and reasoning effort explicitly on every launch."
    },
    "grok": {
      "allowed_spawn_models": [
        "grok-4.3",
        "grok-4.6"
      ],
      "allowed_exec_models": [
        "grok-build-0.1"
      ],
      "forbidden": [],
      "note": "Grok Bot host: native specialist spawns use grok-4.3 (cheap/standard) or grok-4.6 (strong/frontier/escalated). grok-build-0.1 is exec-only until a one-shot helper exists. Pass model and reasoning effort explicitly on every launch. Live transport is Grok Bot Task/executor (GROK.md); scripts/run-grok-specialist.sh --plan is the audit record."
    },
    "cursor": {
      "allowed_spawn_models": [
        "composer-2.5-fast",
        "gpt-5.6-sol-medium",
        "cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast",
        "claude-opus-5-thinking-high"
      ],
      "forbidden": [
        "inherit"
      ],
      "note": "Cursor Agent host: native specialist spawns use Task-tool slugs from config/runtimes/cursor.json. inherit is forbidden. Live transport is Cursor Task (CURSOR.md); scripts/run-cursor-specialist.sh --plan is the audit record. Cloud Task is opt-in and does not replace local cold review."
    }
  },
  "manual_experiments": [],
  "tiers": [
    "cheap",
    "standard",
    "strong",
    "frontier",
    "escalated"
  ],
  "execution_profiles": {
    "granular-ui-fast": {
      "description": "Fast first-pass implementation for a bounded, text-only change to one existing frontend surface.",
      "allowed_workflows": [
        "execute-plan"
      ],
      "first_attempt_only": true,
      "requires_all": [
        "existing_frontend_surface",
        "single_component_or_style_boundary",
        "text_only_inputs",
        "known_local_validation_command"
      ],
      "disqualify_when": [
        "new_feature_or_architecture",
        "new_state_api_navigation_or_contract",
        "new_dependency_or_generated_files",
        "cross_coder_seam",
        "auth_data_money_or_irreversible_effect",
        "image_or_visual_fidelity_judgment",
        "critic_revision_or_retry",
        "broad_or_ambiguous_scope"
      ],
      "fallback": "role_default"
    }
  },
  "roles": {
    "conductor": {
      "agent": "The Conductor",
      "default_tier": "strong",
      "allowed": [
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": false,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "hard_adjudication",
        "conflicting_specialists",
        "second_critic_loop",
        "checkpoint_decision"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "routing_only",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "challenger": {
      "agent": "The Challenger",
      "default_tier": "strong",
      "allowed": [
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "second_critic_loop",
        "prior_review_missed_issue"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "low_risk_docs_review_with_frontier_followup"
      ],
      "note": "Cold review is bought by FRESH CONTEXT, not by model identity (Robin, 2026-09-16). A reviewer that has not seen the design argued gives real objections whether or not it shares a model with the author; rheo-stream measured a same-model reviewer finding 9 blockers where the differing-tier one found 1 at the same cost. What matters is that QA runs on a sufficiently capable tier and escalates on demonstrated need. fresh_context_required stays true and is the real invariant."
    },
    "architect": {
      "agent": "The Architect",
      "default_tier": "strong",
      "allowed": [
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "critic_finds_design_gap",
        "irreversible_data_model",
        "novel_architecture",
        "second_challenger_rejection"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "small_plan_revision",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "mage": {
      "agent": "The Mage",
      "default_tier": "strong",
      "allowed": [
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "allowed_profiles": [
        "granular-ui-fast"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "animation_or_layout_bug",
        "complex_state",
        "design_fidelity_failure",
        "mobile_web_split",
        "second_challenger_rejection"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "small_component_patch",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "analyst": {
      "agent": "Analizer 2000",
      "default_tier": "standard",
      "allowed": [
        "cheap",
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "fuzzy_product_boundary",
        "huge_scope",
        "regulated_domain",
        "second_challenger_rejection"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "narrow_existing_plan",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "cleric": {
      "agent": "The Cleric",
      "default_tier": "strong",
      "allowed": [
        "cheap",
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "ambiguous_design_handoff",
        "manifest_extraction_failed",
        "second_challenger_rejection",
        "subtle_visual_drift"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "straightforward_manifest_ingest",
        "budget_pressure"
      ],
      "note": "The Cleric drives design-taste-frontend (tasteskill) and impeccable, so it is a thinker on the strong tier (Robin, 2026-09-16). Design direction and the pre-ship quality gate are judgement work, not handoff transcription."
    },
    "spellwright": {
      "agent": "The Spellwright",
      "default_tier": "standard",
      "allowed": [
        "cheap",
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "incoherent_after_one_fix",
        "many_cross_repo_dependencies",
        "second_challenger_rejection"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "approved_single_repo_plan",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "counselor": {
      "agent": "The Counselor",
      "default_tier": "standard",
      "allowed": [
        "cheap",
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "legal_medical_political_copy",
        "second_challenger_rejection",
        "sensitive_audience"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "routine_copy_review",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "scribe": {
      "agent": "The Scribe",
      "default_tier": "standard",
      "allowed": [
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": false,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "complex_revision",
        "long_draft",
        "promotion_authority_step",
        "second_challenger_rejection"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "outline_only",
        "format_only"
      ]
    },
    "systemsmith": {
      "agent": "The Systemsmith",
      "default_tier": "strong",
      "allowed": [
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "auth",
        "data_integrity",
        "idempotency",
        "migrations",
        "money_or_credit",
        "permissions",
        "second_challenger_rejection"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "read_only_contract_audit",
        "small_controller_patch",
        "budget_pressure"
      ],
      "note": "The Systemsmith is a thinker, not a grunt: it writes production code over durable state, which is where this campaign's pair-shaped defects are authored (Robin, 2026-09-16). A cheaper coder moves cost sideways into fix rounds \u2014 rheo-stream 0c2 bounced 5 of 5 chunks, 12 coder spawns for five chunks, and each bounce costs a spawn plus a review. second_challenger_rejection escalates it a rung further."
    },
    "mechanic": {
      "agent": "The Mechanic",
      "default_tier": "standard",
      "allowed": [
        "cheap",
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "database_restore_or_migration",
        "irreversible_infra",
        "prod_deploy",
        "second_challenger_rejection",
        "secret_handling"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "local_build_or_smoke_test",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "witness": {
      "agent": "The Witness",
      "default_tier": "standard",
      "allowed": [
        "cheap",
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "huge_log_volume",
        "many_installs_first_pass_thin"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "routine_briefing",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "tally": {
      "agent": "Tally",
      "default_tier": "standard",
      "allowed": [
        "cheap",
        "standard"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": true,
      "escalate_when": [],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "trivial_lookup",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "scoot": {
      "agent": "Scoot",
      "default_tier": "cheap",
      "allowed": [
        "cheap"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": true,
      "escalate_when": [],
      "deescalate_when": []
    },
    "coupler": {
      "agent": "The Coupler",
      "default_tier": "standard",
      "allowed": [
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "repro_failure_needs_deep_trace",
        "second_challenger_rejection",
        "security_critical_seam"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "routine_ui_api_smoke",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "notary": {
      "agent": "The Notary",
      "default_tier": "strong",
      "allowed": [
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "high_stakes_sealed_artifact",
        "irreversible_decision_under_review"
      ],
      "deescalate_when": [
        "low_risk_docs_attestation",
        "budget_pressure"
      ]
    },
    "delegate": {
      "agent": "The Delegate",
      "default_tier": "strong",
      "allowed": [
        "standard",
        "strong",
        "frontier",
        "escalated"
      ],
      "fresh_context_required": true,
      "lock": false,
      "escalate_when": [
        "challenger_blocker_fix_thin",
        "scope_or_cost_change",
        "two_valid_approaches_robins_call",
        "sensitive_system",
        "production_or_public_action",
        "destructive_or_irreversible",
        "unresolved_blocker_or_revision_cap",
        "unexpected_scope_expansion",
        "spec_compliant_but_doctrine_violating"
      ],
      "cold_reviewer": {
        "rule": "capable_tier_fresh_context",
        "tier": "strong",
        "escalate_on": {
          "prior_review_missed_issue": "escalated",
          "second_critic_loop": "escalated"
        },
        "note": "The per-checkpoint cold reviewer runs on a capable tier in a FRESH CONTEXT and does not vary with the author's model (Robin, 2026-09-16). Independence is bought by isolation: a reviewer that has never seen the design argued gives real objections whether or not it shares a model with the coder. rheo-stream 0c2 measured it \u2014 an opus reviewer found 9 blockers where a fable reviewer found 1 on the same artifacts at the same cost, so routing by difference was buying nothing. What matters is that QA is sufficiently capable and that escalation follows a demonstrated miss rather than identity. The Delegate passes the tier's model via BUREAU_REVIEWER_MODEL and logs a MODEL-OVERRIDE when it differs from roles.delegate.model."
      }
    }
  },
  "escalation_ladder": {
    "rule": "first_rejection_then_second",
    "applies_to": "the role that produced the rejected work \u2014 the FIXER, not the reviewer",
    "rungs": [
      {
        "on": "first_challenger_rejection",
        "target": "strong"
      },
      {
        "on": "second_challenger_rejection",
        "target": "escalated"
      }
    ],
    "note": "Robin, 2026-09-16. A bounce is evidence the work item is harder than assumed, and the role that produced it is where that difficulty lives \u2014 so the FIXER escalates, not the reviewer. Targets are named rather than expressed as 'one rung up', because 'one rung' has to be inferred from the tier order and a role already at strong then has two possible readings. A role whose default already meets or exceeds a rung's target stays where it is. Declared here AND in docs/model-routing-and-cast.md; the Conductor and Delegate apply it at specialist retry dispatch and log a MODEL-OVERRIDE naming the trigger. This replaces the older 'bounce rule, one rung on the second rejection', which named no target tier."
  }
}
